# Deliberately (almost) empty — and the reason is worth keeping on file.
#
# On 2026-09-04/05 this file carried two merge attributes for the research lanes' shared files:
# `src/domain/market-events-data.ts merge=market-events` (a custom object-level driver, #1324) and
# `docs/research/forward-tests.md merge=union` (#1334). Both worked exactly as designed for a LOCAL
# `git merge` and changed nothing on GitHub, whose server-side merge runs no custom driver and
# honours no merge attribute (a request to support merge=union has sat open since 2021). 12 of 14
# open research PRs still read `dirty` the morning after both landed.
#
# Issue #1449 removed the shared files instead: the calendar is one JSON file per event under
# src/domain/market-events/, the forward-test register is one markdown fragment per event under
# docs/research/forward-tests/, and each research lane writes only the files its own event id
# names. Plain git merges that every time, server-side included. If you are reaching for a merge
# attribute or driver to fix a recurring conflict, the lesson is that the conflict is a shared
# aggregate with many owners — split it (docs/LESSONS.md, 2026-09-05).
